[Music]  good evening welcome to washington i'm  mike emanuel in for bret baer breaking  tonight we're covering a number of big  stories the death rate is rising at the  site of the collapsed condo towers in  south florida  much of that state is also bracing for  what could be damaging rain and winds  from  tropical storm possibly hurricane elsa  president biden is urging americans who  have not been vaccinated to take the  shot  and says the delta variant of the  coronavirus may be more dangerous  than the original but we begin tonight  with america's crime  crisis a bloody fourth of july weekend  ended with at least  267 people killed in shooting incidents  in chicago 18 people were killed in  shootings involving at least 100 people  police say in nearly all the incidents  no suspects were taken into custody  in cleveland 11 people were shot in a  five hour period  eight people were killed in philadelphia  with 27 others hurt  denver police reported five separate  shootings within a four hour period  in new york embattled governor andrew  cuomo is taking a drastic step due to  the growing gun violence  correspondent brian yennis reports  tonight from times square good evening  brian mike good evening tonight new york  is in a state of emergency the state  will now treat surging gun violence  as a public health crisis the governor  noting today  that over the july 4 weekend more people  died from shootings in his state  than from covet 19. so today  first state in the nation is going to  declare a disaster  emergency on gun violence  governor andrew cuomo declaring a state  of emergency a move that will commit  more money to combating what he calls an  epidemic of gun violence  shootings in new york city are up 42  percent compared to last year  including brazen and random attacks in  times square and on sidewalks in broad  daylight  26 people were shot in two dozen  shootings this weekend alone  about 50 of our shootings are gang or  crew related right now  and we also have an increase in  retaliatory shootings so  one person or two people are shot and  then someone from that side is now  retaliating  the atf led fox news into their new york  city gun vault where  row after row of confiscated rifles and  handguns are stored from crime  scenes scattered citywide the atf and  nypd are working together to combat gun  violence  this is the whole city right now fox  news received an exclusive look  inside their new shared headquarters  where agents are using a new analytics  dashboard to seamlessly share intel  in real time about guns recovered from  crime scenes  shooting investigations and shooting  deaths it's an unprecedented effort to  get guns  used to commit crimes off the streets  while identifying gun traffickers  they hope this will be a model for  cities nationwide  we have to have a rapid tracing of  ballistics to make sure that we're  somebody who gets caught with a gun if  that gun was used in a prior shooting  they were able to rapidly connect it to  that prior crime scene  so we can hold those people accountable  when a firearm is recovered  we submitted for a tracing and we get  the results in a matter of  like a week to 10 days it used to be  much longer time span  the nypd made a record 2300 gun arrests  so far this year  that's a 39 percent increase compared to  last year  nypd commissioner dermot shea says  though the problem is that about 83  percent of those arrested on gun charges  are released back onto the streets he  blames in part  the city's bail reform law passed in  2019.  mike brian yena starting us off in times  square brian many thanks

